Privacy Policy for SlopCheck
Last updated: 01.10.2026

SlopCheck checks reference lists against Crossref. It runs only when you select text on a page (or paste it into the extension) and choose "SlopCheck: verify selected references".

What is processed. The text you select, the DOIs and links in it, and, for references without a working DOI, the citation text. These are sent to Crossref (api.crossref.org and doi.org) only to verify the references. Crossref receives your IP address as part of any web request and handles it under its own privacy policy.

What we do not do. We do not collect, store or receive your data. Nothing is sent to the developer or to any other third party. We do not sell data, use it for advertising, or use it for credit or lending decisions. We do not track your browsing history, clicks or keystrokes, and we do not collect personal information.

Local storage. The extension stores only a counter (date and number of scans used today) in your browser, to apply a daily free-scan limit. It never leaves your device.

Contact. slopcheck@gmail.com

We may update this policy; the date above shows the latest version.
